ALSA: hda/tas2781: accept V1 calibration data without CRC

Lenovo factory calibration blobs written before the CRC scheme carry
neither timestamp nor CRC; both words are zero. The V1 parser rejects
such blobs with "V1 CRC error" and the amplifier protection runs
uncalibrated. Accept a V1 blob whose timestamp and CRC words are both
zero and whose data is non-empty.

Observed on the Lenovo Yoga Slim 7 14APU8 (83AA): EFI variable
CALI_DATA holds four valid 20-byte device blocks followed by zeroed
timestamp and CRC words.

--- a/sound/hda/codecs/side-codecs/tas2781_hda.c
+++ b/sound/hda/codecs/side-codecs/tas2781_hda.c
@@ -139,9 +139,18 @@
 		 */
 		crc = crc32(~0, data, 84) ^ ~0;
 		if (crc != tmp_val[21]) {
-			cali_data->total_sz = 0;
-			dev_err(p->dev, "%s: V1 CRC error\n", __func__);
-			return;
+			/*
+			 * Factory blobs written before the CRC scheme have
+			 * zero in both the timestamp and CRC words. Accept
+			 * them if the data itself is non-empty.
+			 */
+			if (tmp_val[20] || tmp_val[21] || !tmp_val[0]) {
+				cali_data->total_sz = 0;
+				dev_err(p->dev, "%s: V1 CRC error\n", __func__);
+				return;
+			}
+			dev_info(p->dev, "%s: V1 data without CRC, accepted\n",
+				 __func__);
 		}
 
 		for (j = p->ndev - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
